.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-agree-sm2 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-agree\-sm2 \- Run an SM2 key agreement with a slot\*(Aqs key (firmware runs the SM2 KDF)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-agree\-sm2\fR <\fB\-\-peer\-static\fR> <\fB\-\-peer\-ephemeral\fR> [\fB\-\-role\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-len\fR] [\fB\-\-user\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-peer\-id\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISLOT\fR> <\fIKEY_OUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run an SM2 key agreement with a slot\*(Aqs key (firmware runs the SM2 KDF)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-static\fR \fI<PEER_STATIC>\fR
File containing the peer\*(Aqs static public key (65\-byte uncompressed SEC1 point)
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-ephemeral\fR \fI<PEER_EPHEMERAL>\fR
File containing the peer\*(Aqs ephemeral public key (same format)
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fI<ROLE>\fR [default: initiator]
Protocol role
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
initiator
.IP \(bu 2
responder
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-len\fR \fI<KEY_LEN>\fR [default: 16]
Requested session\-key length in bytes (1\-128)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\-id\fR \fI<USER_ID>\fR
Own identity as hex (1\-32 bytes; default: the firmware default)
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-id\fR \fI<PEER_ID>\fR
Peer identity as hex (1\-32 bytes; default: the firmware default)
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN code (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISLOT\fR>
PIV slot holding an SM2 key
.TP
<\fIKEY_OUTPUT\fR>
File to write the session key to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout)
